# Configuration Reference

Opsora CLI uses environment variables for configuration. Set them in `~/.opsora_env` (or pass via shell):

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `OPSORA_PROVIDER_ORDER` | `alibaba,nvidia,bedrock,local` | Comma-separated list of providers to try in order. Valid values: `nvidia`, `alibaba`, `model_studio`, `openai`, `bedrock`, `tokenhub`, `opsora_api`, `local`. |
| `OPSORA_OLLAMA_URL` | `http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1` | Base URL for local Ollama instance. |
| `OPSORA_ALLOW_LOCAL_FALLBACK` | `false` | If `true`, fallback to Ollama when all remote providers fail. |
| `AWS_PROFILE` | `default` | AWS profile name for Bedrock access. |
| `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` | `us-east-1` | AWS region for Bedrock. |

> ⚠️ Never commit `.opsora_env`. It's gitignored by default.

---

# Verification & Troubleshooting

After installation, verify setup:

```bash
opsora --version  # e.g., opsora v3.0.0
opsora --help     # shows CLI flags and options
```

Common issues and fixes:

| Symptom | Likely Cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| `Provider not found: nvidia` | `NVIDIA_API_KEY` missing or invalid | Check `~/.opsora_env`; test with `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $NVIDIA_API_KEY" https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/models` |
| `Ollama unreachable` | Ollama not running or URL misconfigured | Run `ollama serve` or update `OPSORA_OLLAMA_URL` |
| `No models available` | No provider configured or all unavailable | Run `opsora /status` to check live provider status |
| `Permission denied` on file tools | Workspace path outside `/root` | Ensure `WORKSPACE_ROOT` is writable; avoid `~` in paths |

---

# CLI Command Reference

Opsora supports both interactive slash commands and CLI flags:

## Flags

| Flag | Example | Description |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `--version` | `opsora --version` | Show version and exit |
| `--help` | `opsora --help` | Show usage and flags |
| `--session <id>` | `opsora --session my-work` | Load or create named session |
| `--no-approval` | `opsora --no-approval` | Disable confirmation prompts for safe operations |
| `--yolo` | `opsora --yolo` | Enable YOLO mode (auto-execute safe tools) |

## Interactive Commands

| Command | Alias | Description |
|---------|-------|-------------|
| `/status` | — | Show real-time provider availability, model counts, and tool status |
| `/models` | — | List all available models per provider |
| `/model <provider>` | — | Switch active provider (e.g., `/model nvidia`) |
| `/model <p> <m>` | — | Switch to specific model (e.g., `/model alibaba qwen-max`) |
| `/clear` | — | Clear terminal screen |
| `/new` | — | Reset conversation context |
| `/agents` | — | List agent files in workspace |
| `/aws <args>` | — | Run read-only AWS CLI commands (e.g., `/aws ec2 describe-instances --region us-west-2`) |
| `/run <cmd>` | — | Execute shell command (e.g., `/run ls -la`) |
| `/read <file>` | — | Read file (e.g., `/read README.md`) |
| `/graphify <q>` | — | Query knowledge graph (e.g., `/graphify "how does auto-routing work?"`) |
| `/memory <q>` | — | Search persistent memory (e.g., `/memory "API keys"`) |
| `/exit` | — | Exit Opsora CLI |

> 💡 Tip: Use tab completion for `/` commands and file paths.
